I can help — here’s a concise guide and next steps so we can compute CAC and LTV and build the finance narrative. Tell me which option you want (I can draft/send an email to marketing/finance to collect data, or run the numbers if you supply the missing inputs).

1) Key formulas (simple cohort approach)
- CAC = (Total Sales & Marketing spend during period) / (Number of new customers acquired in that period)
- Customer lifetime (months) = 1 / monthly churn rate
- LTV (gross margin basis) = ARPU (monthly) * gross margin % * Customer lifetime
  - ARPU = Average Revenue per User (monthly)
  - gross margin % = contribution margin on revenue (revenue minus variable costs) / revenue
- LTV : CAC ratio = LTV / CAC
- CAC payback (months) = CAC / (ARPU * gross margin %)

Notes:
- Use the same time window for spend and customer acquisitions (e.g., monthly, quarterly).
- For longer horizon or enterprise customers, use cohort / discounted cash flow LTV.

2) Data I need from you (or from finance/marketing)
- Time period to analyze (monthly, last quarter, last 12 months)
- Sales & marketing spend for that period (ad spend + S&M salaries + agency fees, etc.)
- Number of new customers acquired in that period
- ARPU (average revenue per customer) for same period (monthly or annual)
- Gross margin % (or variable cost per customer)
- Monthly churn rate (or retention curve by month)
- If you want discounted LTV: discount rate

3) Quick example (illustrative)
Assume:
- ARPU = $200/month
- Gross margin = 70%
- Monthly churn = 4% → lifetime = 1 / 0.04 = 25 months
- S&M spend = $150,000/month
- New customers = 500/month

Calculations:
- CAC = 150,000 / 500 = $300
- LTV = 200 * 0.70 * 25 = $3,500
- LTV:CAC = 3,500 / 300 ≈ 11.7
- CAC payback = 300 / (200 * 0.70) ≈ 2.14 months

Interpretation:
- LTV:CAC > 3 is commonly desirable for scaling; payback under 12 months is often preferred for fast growth. Customize thresholds for your business model.

4) Suggested finance narrative bullets for stakeholders
- Current liquidity & runway: $5.2M cash, 14 months runway at $62K/month burn (confirm whether burn includes S&M or not)
- Revenue momentum: $1.8M last quarter (show YoY/quarter trends)
- Unit economics: present CAC, LTV, LTV:CAC ratio, CAC payback months (with assumptions)
- Actionable asks: tighten CAC if LTV:CAC below target; increase retention to improve LTV; optimize channel mix to lower CAC; reforecast runway under scenarios (base/growth/conservative)
- Recommendation: present a short plan to reach LTV:CAC target, timeline to profitability, and headcount/spend implications

5) I can draft an email to finance/marketing to collect the missing inputs. Sample (ready to send — I can draft it into your drafts or send it now):
Subject: Request — inputs to compute CAC & LTV (for finance narrative)
Body:
Hi [Name],
I’m preparing the unit-economics section for our finance narrative (runway and growth planning). Can you please send the following for the period [e.g., last quarter / last 12 months]:
- Total sales & marketing spend (breakdown: ad spend vs. S&M salaries vs. agencies)
- Number of new customers acquired
- Average revenue per customer (monthly or ARPU)
- Gross margin % or variable cost per customer
- Monthly churn rate (or retention by month for cohorts)
If you can send this by [date], I’ll produce CAC, LTV, LTV:CAC, CAC payback, and scenario runs for leadership.
Thanks,
[Your name]

Next steps — pick one:
- I’ll draft that email for you (saved to drafts) — tell me recipient and desired send date.
- I’ll send it now — tell me recipient and any edits.
- Or give me the missing metrics and I’ll compute CAC/LTV and produce the narrative + numbersheet.

Which do you want to do?

