Got it — I see from memory that you’re planning a family trip to Italy next month and you need internal financial materials for Horizon Media (cash $5.2M, runway 14 months, burn $62K/month, revenue last quarter $1.8M). How would you like me to help right now? A few options I can do immediately:

- Calculate CAC and LTV (I’ll need a few additional inputs — see list below).
- Draft an internal finance summary / narrative for leadership that includes runway, burn, revenue, and CAC/LTV once computed.
- Draft an investor update or slide text summarizing the financial position and growth metrics.
- Or something else — tell me.

If you want CAC and LTV, please provide (or tell me if you want me to use assumptions):
- Marketing + sales spend for the period you want to measure (e.g., last quarter or last 12 months)
- Number of new customers acquired in that same period
- Average revenue per customer (ARPU) or average order value and purchase frequency
- Gross margin (or contribution margin)
- Churn rate or average customer lifespan (if subscription) or expected retention period

Quick reference formulas I’ll use:
- CAC = Total marketing & sales spend / Number of new customers
- LTV (simple, subscription-style) = ARPU * Gross margin (%) / Churn rate
- LTV (transactional) = Avg. order value * Purchase frequency per period * Avg. customer lifespan * Gross margin (%)

Tell me which metric/timeframe you want (quarterly, trailing-12, etc.), and whether to use actuals you provide or a set of reasonable assumptions — then I’ll calculate and can draft the finance narrative or an email for you.

