Got it — I see the memory about Horizon Media (cash $5.2M, 14‑month runway, $62K/month burn, revenue last quarter $1.8M) and that you need help with CAC and LTV for the finance narrative. I can calculate those and/or draft the internal materials or an email to stakeholders. Before I run numbers, here’s what I need and a quick primer so we’re aligned.

What I need from you (small data checklist)
- Period you want to analyze (e.g., last quarter, last 12 months)
- Marketing & sales spend in that period (total acquisition spend)
- Number of new customers acquired in that same period
- Average revenue per customer (ARPU) during the period, or average order value and purchase frequency
- Gross margin (or contribution margin) %
- Churn rate (or retention rate) per period (or average customer lifetime in months/years)
- Any one-off acquisition channels you want separated (paid ads vs organic vs partners)

Quick formulas and interpretation
- CAC = Total acquisition (marketing + sales) spend / Number of new customers acquired
  - Tells you how much you pay to get one new customer.
- Customer Lifetime (in periods) ≈ 1 / churn_rate (if churn measured per period)
- LTV (simple) = ARPU per period × Gross margin % × Customer lifetime (in same periods)
  - Or LTV = (Avg order value × Avg orders per period × Gross margin %) / churn_rate
  - Use gross margin (not revenue) because LTV should reflect contribution margin toward covering CAC and fixed costs.
- LTV : CAC ratio = LTV / CAC — aim for >3:1 as a rule of thumb (depends on business model and payback period)
- Payback period = CAC / (ARPU × Gross margin %) — how many periods (months) to recoup CAC

Example (illustrative; I’ll compute exact numbers once you give data)
- Suppose last quarter acquisition spend = $180k and new customers = 900 → CAC = $200
- Suppose ARPU/month = $50, gross margin = 60%, monthly churn = 4% → lifetime = 1/0.04 = 25 months → LTV = $50 × 0.60 × 25 = $750
- LTV:CAC = 750 / 200 = 3.75 → healthy by the 3:1 rule
- Payback period = 200 / (50×0.60) = 6.67 months

How I can help right now
- Calculate CAC and LTV using your actual numbers (I’ll do the math and show assumptions).
- Create a short one‑page finance narrative (bullet points + simple chart suggestions) you can share with leadership.
- Draft an internal email to the CFO/CEO/board summarizing findings and recommended actions (e.g., adjust marketing spend, focus on retention).
- Prepare slides or a table showing sensitivity (different churn or CAC scenarios).

Tell me which of the following you want me to do next:
1) Calculate CAC & LTV — I’ll need the checklist data you can provide.
2) Draft the one‑page finance narrative or an email to execs (specify recipient and tone).
3) Both (calc + draft materials).

Send the numbers you have (or say “use illustrative assumptions”) and I’ll proceed.

