I see from your memory that you’re preparing internal financial materials for Horizon Media (cash $5.2M, 14‑month runway, burn $62K/month, revenue last quarter $1.8M) and want help with CAC and LTV and the finance narrative. How would you like me to help right now? I can do any of the following — tell me which:

1) Calculate CAC & LTV for you
   - I can compute these if you give me the inputs below (or I can pull related emails/attachments from your inbox if you prefer).
   - Needed inputs:
     - Marketing + sales spend over the period you want to measure (e.g., last 12 months or last quarter)
     - Number of new customers acquired in that period
     - Average revenue per customer per period (ARPU) or avg. order value and purchase frequency
     - Gross margin % (or cost of goods sold) to convert revenue to gross profit
     - Average customer lifetime (in months or years) OR monthly churn rate
   - Formulas I’ll use:
     - CAC = Total marketing & sales spend / Number of new customers
     - LTV (gross) = ARPU × Gross margin % × Average customer lifetime (in same time units)
     - LTV : CAC ratio = LTV / CAC
   - If you want, I can run scenarios (best/likely/worst) and produce short talking points for your narrative.

2) Draft an email to request missing data or align stakeholders
   - Example subject: Request: Marketing & CAC/LTV inputs for finance deck
   - Example body (editable):
     Hi [Name],
     
     I’m finalizing the internal finance deck and need the following inputs to calculate CAC and LTV for Horizon Media:
     - Marketing + sales spend (last 12 months and last quarter)
     - Number of new customers acquired (same periods)
     - Avg. revenue per customer (ARPU) or avg. order value and purchase frequency
     - Gross margin %
     - Average customer lifetime or churn rate
     
     Can you share these by EOD [date]? If you have an existing spreadsheet or report, please attach it.
     
     Thanks,
     [Your name]
   - Tell me who to send it to and whether to send now or save as a draft.

3) Search your inbox for relevant emails or attachments (e.g., “marketing spend report,” “customer acquisition data,” “Q4 revenue breakdown”) and summarize findings.

4) Draft the finance narrative and slides bullets based on current numbers (cash runway, burn, revenue trends) and assumptions for CAC/LTV scenarios.

Which option would you like? If it’s calculation (1), paste the input numbers or tell me to search your inbox for them. If it’s drafting/sending (2), give recipients and whether to send or draft.

